-- title:
--   The two branches of the crossing model are distinct
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring and let $\pi \in W$, and suppose that the quotient ring $W/(\pi)$ is nontrivial, i.e. $\pi$ is not a unit in $W$. Work in the crossing model $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\ W\ \pi$, defined as the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\ 2)\ W$ — that is, $W[[X_0,X_1]]$ — by the ideal `uvCrossingIdeal` generated by the single element $X_0X_1 - \pi$, where $\pi$ denotes the constant power series with value $\pi$. The theorem asserts that the element $V\ \pi$ of this quotient ring does not lie in the principal ideal generated by the element $U\ \pi$: in symbols, $V\,\pi \notin (U\,\pi)$ as an ideal of $W[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1-\pi)$. Here $U$ and $V$ are the two distinguished elements of the crossing model attached to $\pi$, cutting out its two branches. The nontriviality of $W/(\pi)$ is essential: if $\pi$ were a unit the two branches would coincide and the conclusion would fail.
--
--   This is the incomparability of the two branches of the ordinary double point $W[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi)$: neither branch divides the other, so $(U\,\pi)$ and $(V\,\pi)$ are genuinely two distinct ideals. It is used in the analysis of the local structure of a modular curve at a node of its special fibre, in the construction of the branch and centre places attached to a crossing presentation at an Igusa end.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_V_notMem_span_U.lean

